                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e5990707-93cd-381b-954c-c7f183531485",
                        "entry_id": "ce1887f6-96c8-3a5a-8261-a89303d987ca",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Related to or characterised by navel-gazing (omphaloskepsis)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable",
                            "uncommon"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "516b119a-fb14-46b8-aaf8-78b23b8f16d2",
                                "sense_id": "e5990707-93cd-381b-954c-c7f183531485",
                                "text": "The hypnotic method, he added, was used by the sculptors of antiquity to make their models hold still, by the “omphalopsychic” monks of Mount Athos staring at their navel, by Indian fakirs converging their eyes on the tip of their nose, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "949a5ca2-129f-49ee-ac24-1a54a8dd1939",
                                "sense_id": "e5990707-93cd-381b-954c-c7f183531485",
                                "text": "This also seems to suggest that Alcibiades was primarily in love with Socrates’ personality, his harmonious nature, which nevertheless fulfilled itself in a negative self-relation to the idea and an omphalopsychic staring at oneself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a6cac2ca-c0b5-45f8-bca5-65e590d40cc7",
                                "sense_id": "e5990707-93cd-381b-954c-c7f183531485",
                                "text": "Reflexivity has become a decidedly fashionable subject in social anthropoogy since the mid-1980s, though it is still quite common for reflexivity to be thought of as either involving any autobiographical comments whatsoever or as omphalopsychic irrelevance (or both)."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "a23194f2-2f37-397e-a431-e879e9da5245",
                "word": "omphalopsychic",
